# Normalizer-orbit data and kernel-cheap checkers, q=2 twin (normalizer-orbit partition, part A)

The q=2 (`SmallGroup(3125,69)` / `Coordinate 2`) mirror of
`Twin1/NormOrbitData.lean`. For each of the 148 subgroup-class representatives
`H = reps r`, the compiled generator (`Generators/Twin2/NormGen.lean`) emits, as
untrusted data re-checked here by kernel `decide`, the normalizer index, the
abelianized-conjugation matrices, the induced character permutation, the orbit
labels and the BFS spanning-tree witnesses.

Twin note: `normIdxData` is byte-identical to q=1 (normalizers are the same
subgroup indices); `normMats`/`normActPos`/`normLabel`/tree data are regenerated
from the q=2 group law and diverge on the 34 reshaped k≤3 reps, but the aggregate
orbit total (2724) and the order-fibre split ({148,2376,200}) are identical.

The checkers here are pure `ZMod 25` matrix arithmetic and `Nat` bookkeeping — no
sift. `NormOrbits.lean` assembles the whole-range checks and the aggregate counts.
-/

-- machine-emitted data: silence style linters (generated long lines, file-level options)
set_option linter.style.longLine false

namespace LeanDring.P5Presentation.Q2

open Fin.NatCast

set_option maxRecDepth 100000
-- file-level maxHeartbeats: dozens of decide-heavy declarations below need it
set_option linter.style.setOption false
set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000

/-- Matrix action on a character exponent vector: `(M e)_i = dotZ (row_i) e`. -/
def actVecZ (M : List (List (ZMod 25))) (e : List (ZMod 25)) : List (ZMod 25) :=
  M.map (fun row => dotZ row e)

/-- Additive order (`1`, `5` or `25`) of a character exponent vector. -/
def charOrdZ (e : List (ZMod 25)) : Nat :=
  25 / (e.foldl (fun acc z => Nat.gcd acc z.val) 25)

